olitan area and in Virginia, after neighboring cities Virginia Beach and Chesapeake, as well as the 101st-most populous city in the United States. The city holds a strategic position as the historical, urban, financial, and cultural center of the Hampton Roads area, which has more than 1.8 million inhabitants and is the 37th-largest metropolitan area in the U.S.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/The_Wisconsin_Battleship_in_Norfolk%2C_VA.jpg/330px-The_Wisconsin_Battleship_in_Norfolk%2C_VA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norfolk%2C_Virginia"},"twins":["Q44160","Q3857","Q188806","Q1829","Q2141","Q1645","Q23109"],"climate":{"temp":[4.2,5.2,8.5,13.9,19,24.2,26.6,25.9,23,17.5,11.4,7],"rain":[73,72,85,88,98,113,131,138,130,104,82,91],"cloud":[56,57,56,53,55,55,54,53,53,47,47,56]}}